<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Well</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as wells</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A well is a shaft dug into the ground to reach water, essential for life and travel in arid regions such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahara">Sahara</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>. Control of wells determined which routes caravans and armies could use. The Kanem-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu Empire</a> profile notes that the construction of wells along routes enhanced the operational effectiveness of its armies.</p></div>
